==Spanish==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|es|bacallao}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|it|nl|bakaliaw}}, {{m|odt|bakeljauw}}, {{m|odt|kabeljauw}}, of {{unk|it|title=uncertain}} origin.  Possibly from {{der|it|la|baculum||stick, staff}}, referring to the way cod were split and dried on wooden sticks.  Or, possibly borrowed or influenced by {{bor|es|eu|bakailao}}, which could be related to the Dutch word.

Cognate to Italian {{m|it|baccalà}}, Portuguese {{m|pt|bacalhau}}, Galician {{m|gl|bacallau}}, Catalan {{m|ca|bacallà}}.

